.KEY DIR/A,STEP/K,REMOTE/K
.BRA {
.KET }
; Claude install: C:Claude, C:ClaudeCode and C:uptelnet. It stands alone: nothing here
; needs UP-Term, and nothing here looks at an UP-Term: assign (that would ask for the volume).
; Run by this archive's Install (an Installer script), which asks the questions:
;   Execute <archive>/Files/install.dos <archive>/Files [STEP <part>]
; From a Shell without Installer the same line installs everything. The Installer
; runs the parts one at a time with STEP (tests/test_dist_addons.py holds the two to
; the same list); the first part, check, has nothing to check for a stand-alone archive.
FailAt 21
; the archive's Files drawer: every name below is relative to it
CD "{DIR}"
; REMOTE "host port": ENVARC:Claude/remote, where Claude Code runs (the NAS); plain
; Claude, with no API key, connects there. Written whenever given (ENVARC: and ENV:).
; The Installer passes it in the variable file ENV:UPTOPTREMOTE (as the base's
; Install does its options: a long path made the command line too long).
Set optremote "{REMOTE}"
If NOT "{STEP}" EQ ""
  If EXISTS ENV:UPTOPTREMOTE
    Set optremote "$UPTOPTREMOTE"
  EndIf
EndIf
If NOT "{STEP}" EQ ""
  Skip {STEP}
EndIf
; @include dist/common/@CHECKFRAG@
Lab claude
; C:Claude, the native Claude client (README), and C:ClaudeCode: Claude Code on the
; NAS through C:uptelnet (this archive's copy: the same program as UP-Term.lha's; no
; ixemul); a script, so the s bit makes it a command.
; Its talking to Anthropic needs AmiSSL 5; ENVARC:Claude is where its settings go
; (Install never writes a key).
Copy Claude C:Claude CLONE QUIET
Copy ClaudeCode C:ClaudeCode CLONE QUIET
Protect C:ClaudeCode +s QUIET
Copy uptelnet C:uptelnet CLONE QUIET
If NOT EXISTS ENVARC:Claude
  MakeDir ENVARC:Claude
EndIf
If NOT "$optremote" EQ ""
  ; the chosen value always wins (the Installer's page starts with the
  ; existing file's host and port, so a kept answer is the same line)
  If NOT EXISTS ENV:Claude
    MakeDir ENV:Claude
  EndIf
  Echo >ENVARC:Claude/remote "; Claude Code on another computer: host and port. With no API key,"
  Echo >>ENVARC:Claude/remote "; plain Claude connects there (uptelnet). Delete this file to stop."
  Echo >>ENVARC:Claude/remote "$optremote"
  Copy ENVARC:Claude/remote ENV:Claude/remote CLONE QUIET
EndIf
If NOT "{STEP}" EQ ""
  Quit 0
EndIf
; @include dist/common/record.dos
Echo "Claude installed: type  Claude  in a Shell or an UP-Term window, or double-click ClaudeCode."
